Hi all,
I wanted to share a note about a resource we've been working on that might be of interest to people using mirt. We have standardized over 1000 item response datasets to meet a common data format and made them available directly in R. You can see how they might be used directly with mirt in a simple example here:
https://github.com/ben-domingue/irw/blob/main/manuscript_src/01_simpleIRT.R

More information about this manuscript can be found in this (open access!) article here <https://link.springer.com/article/10.3758/s13428-025-02796-y?_gl=1*y2kyrh*_up*MQ..*_gs*MQ..&gclid=Cj0KCQjw3aLHBhDTARIsAIRij5_XdiuDsoudC128stGdDayfFe89evg1cBJCkP5HMAmVfNUVSqwDiu4aAub2EALw_wcB&gbraid=0AAAAApIS33uBzUvthWhS0PDuvNhct3Vds> or at the project website here <https://itemresponsewarehouse.org/>. Please send any questions you may have my way and a tip of the hat to Phil for making an essential piece of software!

Ben

